 "ui.foot.ratings": "Ratings reflect community consensus for units without special techs. Specialists, unit levels, and pure stat buffs are not taken into account.",
 "ui.foot.techsLabel": "Techs:",
 "ui.foot.techs": "“Confirmed” means the change follows directly from the tech’s game text and the target types (ground/air). For example, a unit that can no longer attack aerial units no longer counters them. “Tendency” means the direction is confirmed, but the strength is unknown. A tech applies to the unit regardless of whether it belongs to you or your opponent.",
 "ui.foot.sources": "Unit and tech names as well as game texts in all languages come from the game files. Target types and tech assignments are checked against the {wiki}, which is also where the unit images come from.",
 "ui.foot.wiki": "Mechabellum Wiki",
 "ui.foot.translation": "All other texts were translated from German with AI and may contain errors.",
 "ui.foot.usage": "Controls: typing letters searches (in all languages), {enter} selects the first match, {esc} clears the search or the selection, and so does clicking an empty spot. Hover over a highlighted tile to see the reason. Entries in the list on the right are clickable, and ⚙ hints turn on that tech. Set language, grouping, theme, size, colors, and sidebar under “View”.",
